1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,440
M: Laurie, don't we have a meeting to attend at 3:30 p.m.?

2
00:00:03,845 --> 00:00:05,500
W: You didn't read your e-mail yet, Steve?

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:12,220
We were all notified that it has been postponed until tomorrow because Mr. Whistler's flight was canceled this morning.

4
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:15,200
M: Oh, I haven't checked my inbox all day long.

5
00:00:15,775 --> 00:00:17,100
W: You'd better take a look at it then.

6
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:21,345
That e-mail contains some important information relevant to the meeting.

7
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:23,860
M: Thanks for letting me know about that.

8
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:28,760
You know, since we have some free time now, we ought to finish doing the employee evaluations.

9
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:29,900
W: I agree.

10
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:33,100
I'll collect the files from my office and be back soon.
